				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				356,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Common): Add 5 IPC channel definitions across Configuration, Extensions, Themes\n\nIntroduce new strongly-typed IPC channel mappings in the `DefineChannels!` macro within the Channel.rs module to support additional frontend-to-backend communication for three service domains:\n\n- Configuration: `ConfigurationInspect` (`\"configuration:inspect\"`) and `ConfigurationLookup` (`\"configuration:lookup\"`) sit between the existing `ConfigurationGet` and `ConfigurationUpdate` channels, enabling introspection and lookup operations on configuration values.\n- Extensions: `ExtensionsGetManifest` (`\"extensions:getManifest\"`) and `ExtensionsResetPinnedState` (`\"extensions:resetPinnedStateForAllUserExtensions\"`) join the Extensions channel group to support manifest retrieval and bulk pin state resets — the latter using a descriptive PascalCase method name that maps to a longer `camelCase` protocol string.\n- Themes: `ThemesGetColorTheme` (`\"themes:getColorTheme\"`) follows `ThemesGetActive`, providing a dedicated channel for fetching the full color theme payload rather than just the active theme identifier.\n\nAlso advance the Documentation/Rust submodule pointer to include the latest documentation updates.\n\nThese channels complete gaps in the IPC protocol surface needed by Wind and Cocoon consumers.",
			"SHA": "db0d8f3428b85274531c491dfc89e52a8115eeed"
		}
